        data-src="path/to/image1.jpg" 
        src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" 
        alt="Project 1"
        width="400" 
        height="300"
      >
    </div>
    <!-- Repeat for other images -->
  </div>
</div>
```

**Key Points:**
- **`width` and `height` attributes**: Always specify these to prevent layout shifts (CLS). This is crucial for performance and Core Web Vitals.
- **`data-src`**: Contains the actual image URL.
- **`src`**: Contains a tiny placeholder (e.g., a 1x1 transparent GIF) to maintain the aspect ratio.
- **`lazy` class**: Tells `lazysizes` to monitor this image.

